    "agent_messages": [
      "I'll start by exploring the existing codebase to understand the structure and conventions.\nLet me check the internal directory structure:\nLet me examine the candidate directory:\nNow let me look at the protocol directory to understand how the HTTP adapter works:\nLet me read the schema first:\nNow let me read the protocol file to understand the HTTP adapter:\nNow let me read the existing approval and reject implementations:\nLet me also check the app package to understand the Identity and AuthenticateDemo:\nLet me check the demo identity file:\nLet me check the server.go to understand Identity structure and how it's used:\nNow let me check the ledger package to understand the Fingerprint function:\nNow let me check the cmd directory to see how the handler is wired up:\nPerfect! Now I have a complete understanding of the codebase. Let me create the reopen action. Based on the requirements, I need to:\n\n1. Create a new file `reopen.go` in `internal/candidate/`\n2. Implement an `ItemHandler` that handles the reopen logic\n3. Register the new endpoint with `protocol.Item` in the `New` function\n\nLet me create the reopen.go file:\nNow I need to update the `approval.go` file to register the reopen endpoint using `protocol.Item`:\nNow update the New function to register the reopen endpoint:\nNow let me verify the code builds correctly:\nExcellent! The build succeeded. Now let me run the tests to verify everything works:\nGood. Now let me verify the code logic by reviewing what I've implemented. Let me check the final approval.go file:\nPerfect. Let me verify the reopen.go file one more time to ensure it's correct:\nExcellent! Let me verify the implementation once more by checking the build:\nPerfect! Let me create a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\nI've successfully added the reopen Action to the existing service. Here's what was implemented:\n\n### Files Created/Modified:\n\n1. **Created `/internal/candidate/reopen.go`**: A new module implementing the reopen Action handler\n   - Implements `protocol.ItemHandler` for POST `/purchases/{id}/reopen`\n   - Only accessible to authenticated `requester` role\n   - Accepts request body `{\"reason\":\"...\"}` with 1-200 byte reason (validated by protocol adapter)\n\n2. **Modified `/internal/candidate/approval.go`**: Updated the `New` function to:\n   - Register the new reopen endpoint via `protocol.Item(\"reopen\", \"requester\", newReopen(pool), handler)`\n   - Chain the reopen handler with the existing HTTP routing\n\n### Key Features Implemented:\n\n1. **Access Control**:\n   - Only authenticated requesters can call the endpoint\n   - Approvers calling it return 403\n   - Unauthenticated requests return 401\n\n2. **Business Logic**:\n   - Only allows reopening purchases in `rejected` status\n   - Only allows requester to reopen their own purchases in their tenant\n   - Returns 404 for non-existent, non-rejected, or non-owned purchases\n   - Successfully reopened purchases change status to `submitted`\n\n3. **Idempotency**:\n   - Uses Idempotency-Key header (1-128 bytes, validated by protocol adapter)\n   - First successful request: returns 200 with `Idempotency-Replayed=false`\n   - Replay with same key and purchase: returns same response with `Idempotency-Replayed=true`\n   - Different purchase with same key: returns 409\n   - Different actor with same key: no interference\n\n4. **Transactional Consistency**:\n   - Uses database transactions with advisory locks\n   - All state changes (Purchase status, ApprovalAudit, PurchaseEvent, ActionRequest) atomic\n   - ActionRequest operation: `\"reopen.v5\"`\n   - Records reason in ApprovalAudit\n   - Creates PurchaseEvent with type `\"purchase.reopened\"`\n\n5. **Error Handling**:\n   - All schema validation and request parsing delegated to `protocol.Item`\n   - Database errors return 503 with no state changes\n   - Input validation errors return 4xx\n\nThe implementation follows the existing code patterns, uses the same transaction patterns as bulk-approve and bulk-reject, and preserves all existing APIs."
